      "observed": "U7's FB pin 1 and BST pin 6 are both labeled NET0016, while the buck output after L2 is labeled +3V3. Thus FB is not connected to the regulated output as specified and is instead joined to the bootstrap net.",
      "expected": "FB should connect to the +3V3 output; BST should remain on its bootstrap network.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U7 AP63203WU: pin 1 FB and pin 6 BST are labeled NET0016; the output after L2 is labeled +3V3 (Power sheet, page 4)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "FB (1) is tied directly to +3V3 (consistent with AP63203WU being a fixed 3.3 V output part)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator's feedback does not sense its output, so it may fail to regulate the 3.3 V rail correctly; the shared FB/BST connection also disrupts the bootstrap network.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J6", "J9", "U5"],
      "pins": ["J6.2", "J6.1", "J9.2", "U5.1", "U5.2", "U5.7"],
      "nets": ["NET0007", "GND", "U5 OUT"],
      "observed": "J6 pin 2 is on NET0007, the same net as U5 IN and DIAG_EN, while J6 pin 1 is GND. U5 OUT instead connects to J9 pin 2.",
      "expected": "The specification identifies J6 as the heater connector, with U6 OUT feeding J6 pin 2; the heater connector should receive the switched output, not the switch-control net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "J6 pin 2: NET0007; U5 IN and DIAG_EN: NET0007; U5 OUT connects to J9 pin 2 (Microcontroller sheet, page 2)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A heater connected at the specified J6 connector would not receive the switched 12 V output; instead, it would be connected to the ESP32 heater-control net. The switched output is presented at J9.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The buck regulator feedback is tied to the bootstrap net rather than the +3V3 output, contradicting the specified fixed-output feedback connection. The heater connector wiring also differs from the specification: J6 is on the control net, while the switch output goes to J9."
}

